                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> Any progress on this? It will be sad to go back to `plenary.test_harness` just because of this issue. 😞\r\n\r\nThere is no work done or planned for LuaCov compatibility with 'mini.test', I am afraid. Mostly because I can not reasonably imagine how this would work with the suggested way of running tests (each in a separate child process). ",
